+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+Tasks are added through `TaskList.add`, which validates title, priority and tags and returns a `Result`; domain code in `src/domain/` never throws, reads no clock and makes no random values. `src/index.ts` is the public API and exports `createTodoList` and a few helpers.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- One call imports many lines, reporting each failure with its line number and a reason.
+- Reuse `list.add` so import follows exactly the same validation rules as adding by hand.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Quoted fields or `;` inside titles, other separators, headers, file reading, updating existing tasks, or rolling back a partial import.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Put the code in `src/domain/import.ts` as `importTasks(list: TaskList, text: string): ImportReport`, with TSDoc, and re-export it and its types (`ImportReport`, `RejectedLine`) from `src/index.ts`. It only calls `list.add`, so it needs no clock.
+- Split on `/\r?\n/`; skip lines that are blank after trimming; line numbers come from the index in the split, so blank lines count.
+- Split each line on `;`. More than three fields is rejected (`invalid-input`-style message: too many fields), since a stray `;` would silently shift tags. Fewer than three is accepted.
+- Priority is trimmed and passed as text to `list.add`, which validates it at runtime; a blank priority is omitted so `add` defaults to `normal`. Case is not folded: `High` is rejected as an unknown priority, matching `add`.
+- Tags: trimmed text split on whitespace, empty pieces dropped, passed to `add`, which dedupes and validates.
+- `reason` is the error message from `list.add`'s `Result`, so it says what is wrong. Duplicates, including earlier lines of the same text, fall out of `add`'s duplicate check.
+- Import is not atomic: valid lines are added even if others are rejected, as the request states.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- A title that legitimately contains `;` cannot be imported; it is reported as too many fields rather than mis-parsed.
+- Lines are validated one by one against the live list, so an import may be partially applied; the report tells the caller exactly what was left out.
