+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Teams are moving to Tidy Tasks from their spreadsheets and have tasks to bring along in bulk. Adding them one by one through `add` is slow; a single call that takes spreadsheet-style text is needed.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add a public helper `importTasks(list, text)`, exported from `src/index.ts`.
+- The text holds one task per line, as `title;priority;tags`. The priority may be empty (normal); tags are separated by spaces. Blank lines are skipped.
+- Every valid line is added to the list. The helper returns `{ imported, rejected }`: the number of tasks added, and a `{ line, reason }` entry for each line that could not be added, with `line` counting from 1.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-import`: bulk import of tasks from `title;priority;tags` text into a task list, and the report of what was imported and rejected.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New domain code in `src/domain/import.ts`, a new export in `src/index.ts`, new tests in `test/`.
+- No change to the `TaskList` interface or to existing behavior; no new dependency.
